From dfa79b74ef00449b33caeb06eec776c4ead277ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: superc <superc@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:16:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] superc: T!error functions with try/catch

- 'T!error' suffix on function declarators (before the declarator,
  after a '*' or after the whole declarator), stored in FuncAttr and
  merged across redeclarations.
- 'err(id, msg)' now requires the enclosing function to return
  'T!error' and returns immediately; the no-argument re-raise form is
  gone (use 'try' to forward an error).
- 'try f()' propagates: it clears the error slot, evaluates the call,
  and on failure runs the frame's errdefer/defer and returns the
  sentinel value.  Only usable inside a 'T!error' function.
- 'f() catch e { ... }' handles the error in place: it snapshots the
  error into the handler variable and clears the slot, so consecutive
  handlers cannot see stale state.  The handler must leave by itself.
- A 'T!error' call result must be consumed by 'try' or 'catch';
  dropping it (assignment, operator, condition, return, statement) is
  diagnosed instead of silently losing the error.
- Reset the superc parser state per translation unit so that an error
  longjmp cannot leak into the next tcc state.
- Keyword ids stay aligned with the enum when a keyword name is
  already interned (the x86 'test' mnemonic).
- Tests: 163_superc_try, 164_superc_try_errors; 157/158 updated.
- Drop the accidentally committed .superc-mode build marker.
